20 Before changing power, anolyte flow can be adjusted to match the new target Ni feed flow rate. During the 
initial power on from trickle adjust flow rate based on a 6 000 amp rectifier setting. 
HOW TO DO IT
Anolyte withdrawal flow rate should be equal to the new Ni feed flow rate calculated in step 2. To manually 
adjust the anolyte flow:
• Select the following faceplate for the Separator control valve on the bay you wish to adjust:
o Bay 1: 346-PIC-26614
o Bay 2: 346-PIC-30614
o Bay 3: 346-PIC-32614
o Bay 4: 346-PIC-36614
• Set control valve to AUTO.
• Adjust valve to achieve desired anolyte withdrawal flow rate.
• Set control valve back to CASCADE.
